# Problem

The pages of the fire drill: what you find, and what happens after each
choice you make.

Read a page only when the fire drill sends you to it, since a page read early
gives away what happens next. Each page ends with what to do next: make
another choice, go back to a step of the drill, or end the drill.
cat docs/firedrill/FIREDRILL-0001-customer-charged-twice/solution/README.md
# Solution

What the fire drill expects of you. Read nothing here until the drill is
over.

* `expected-response.md`: the response the playbook leads to in the drill's
  case, step by step.
* `debrief.md`: questions to look back on the drill with, and what the drill
  found wrong or missing in the playbook.
